 "files": [
  {
   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Hologram\n\nA scene played as projected light: a ghost double shimmers off the image, emission lines structure it, a halo spills from bright areas, and everything leans toward its tint. WebGL.\n\nCategory: filters. Length: 3 s. WebGL: yes.\n\nUse when:\n- A feature should present as a projection rather than as a screen: a sci-fi flavoured reveal, a beat about what is coming.\n- The scene is high contrast, since only what is bright enough carries through the projection.\n- You want the projection to materialize on entry: raise intensity from 0 and the scene resolves into light.\n\nAvoid when:\n- The story is a physical display being watched rather than light standing in the air: use crt-screen.\n- You want damage rather than projection: use sustained-glitch.\n\nVariables:\n- tint (color): Tint, default \"#63e8ff\"\n- glow (number, 0-3): Glow, default 1\n- ghost (number, 0-3): Ghost, default 1\n- flicker (number, 0-3): Flicker, default 1\n- intensity (number, 0-1): Intensity, default 1\n- title (string): Title, default \"Deploys this week\"\n- value (string): Value, default \"2,481\"\n- background (color): Scene background, default \"#0a0a0a\"\n- accent (color): Accent, default \"#a1eebd\"\n- resolution (number, 0.25-1): Resolution, default 0.75\n\nSource: https://github.com/Remocn/remocn. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
  {
   "path": "scene.html",
   "role": "source",
   "content": "<!doctype html>\n<!--\n  Hologram\n\n  Play a scene as a projection: ghost double, emission lines, only the bright parts carrying. remocn wraps its children with the experimental HTML-in-Canvas API; a render machine has no such API, so this block draws remocn's preview scene (a stat and eight bars, text from the variables) on a 2D canvas and applies the same shader to it. It does not apply the look to a host's video.\n\n  Ported to an HTML + GSAP sub-composition by usemosio/blocks from:\n  https://github.com/Remocn/remocn/blob/126221ae00ba86eb40b65731b125ff398687d3b7/registry/remocn/hologram/index.tsx\n\n  MIT License\n\n  Copyright (c) 2026 Remocn\n\n  Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy\n  of this software and associated documentation files (the \"Software\"), to deal\n  in the Software without restriction, including without limitation the rights\n  to use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell\n  copies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom the Software is\n  furnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:\n\n  The above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in all\n  copies or substantial portions of the Software.\n\n  THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED \"AS IS\", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR\n  IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,\n  FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE\n  AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER\n  LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM,\n  OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE\n  SOFTWARE.\n-->\n<html\n  lang=\"en\"\n  data-composition-id=\"hologram\"\n  data-composition-duration=\"3\"\n  data-composition-variables='[\n    {\"id\": \"tint\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Tint\", \"description\": \"Colour of the projected light. Sets the whole character.\", \"default\": \"#63e8ff\"},\n    {\"id\": \"glow\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Glow\", \"description\": \"Emission strength: light off the edges of shapes and the halo bright areas throw.\", \"default\": 1, \"min\": 0, \"max\": 3, \"step\": 0.1},\n    {\"id\": \"ghost\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Ghost\", \"description\": \"How unstable the projection is: how far the doubled image sits from the original and how far scanlines slip sideways.\", \"default\": 1, \"min\": 0, \"max\": 3, \"step\": 0.1},\n    {\"id\": \"flicker\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"motion\", \"label\": \"Flicker\", \"description\": \"Depth of the brightness pulse, on a 15-frame cycle with per-frame jitter.\", \"default\": 1, \"min\": 0, \"max\": 3, \"step\": 0.1},\n    {\"id\": \"intensity\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Intensity\", \"description\": \"How much of the effect shows. 0 shows the plain scene.\", \"default\": 1, \"min\": 0, \"max\": 1, \"step\": 0.05},\n    {\"id\": \"title\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Title\", \"description\": \"Small label above the number in the scene.\", \"default\": \"Deploys this week\"},\n    {\"id\": \"value\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Value\", \"description\": \"Large number in the scene.\", \"default\": \"2,481\"},\n    {\"id\": \"background\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Scene background\", \"description\": \"Background of the scene.\", \"default\": \"#0a0a0a\"},\n    {\"id\": \"accent\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Accent\", \"description\": \"Colour of the last bar.\", \"default\": \"#a1eebd\"},\n    {\"id\": \"resolution\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"quality\", \"label\": \"Resolution\", \"description\": \"Share of the frame size the shader is drawn at, then scaled up. Lower renders faster.\", \"default\": 0.75, \"min\": 0.25, \"max\": 1, \"step\": 0.05}\n  ]'\n>\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <title>Hologram</title>\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <template>\n      <link\n        rel=\"stylesheet\"\n        href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Geist:wght@400;500;600;700&amp;display=block\"\n      />\n      <style>\n        #root {\n          position: absolute;\n          inset: 0;\n          overflow: hidden;\n          container-type: size;\n          pointer-events: none;\n          background: #04070d;\n          font-family: var(--font-display, Geist, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, sans-serif);\n        }\n        .hol-stage { position: absolute; inset: 0; }\n        .hol-scene, .hol-canvas { position: absolute; inset: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; display: block; }\n        .hol-scene { display: none; }\n        .hol-off .hol-scene { display: block; }\n        .hol-off .hol-canvas { display: none; }\n      </style>\n\n      <div id=\"root\" data-composition-id=\"hologram\" data-duration=\"3\" data-fps=\"30\">\n        <div id=\"hol-clip\" class=\"hol-stage clip\" data-start=\"0\" data-duration=\"3\" data-track-index=\"0\">\n          <canvas id=\"hol-scene\" class=\"hol-scene\"></canvas>\n          <canvas id=\"hol-canvas\" class=\"hol-canvas\"></canvas>\n        </div>\n\n        <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/gsap@3.14.2/dist/gsap.min.js\"></script>\n        <script>\n          (function () {\n            \"use strict\";\n            var root = document.getElementById(\"root\");\n            var vars =\n              window.__hyperframes && window.__hyperframes.getVariables\n                ? window.__hyperframes.getVariables()\n                : {};\n\n            function num(value, fallback, min, max) {\n              var n = Number(value);\n              return Number.isFinite(n) ? Math.min(max, Math.max(min, n)) : fallback;\n            }\n            function str(value, fallback) {\n              return typeof value === \"string\" && value.trim() ? value : fallback;\n            }\n            function pick(value, list, fallback) {\n              return list.indexOf(String(value)) >= 0 ? String(value) : fallback;\n            }\n            function bool(value, fallback) {\n              return typeof value === \"boolean\" ? value : value === \"true\" ? true : value === \"false\" ? false : fallback;\n            }\n            \n            var total = parseFloat(root.dataset.duration || \"3\");\n            var NAME = \"hologram\";\n            var stage = document.getElementById(\"hol-clip\");\n            var canvas = document.getElementById(\"hol-canvas\");\n            var scene = document.getElementById(\"hol-scene\");\n            function hex(value, fallback) {\n              var m = /^#?([0-9a-f]{3}|[0-9a-f]{6})$/i.exec(String(value || \"\").trim());\n              if (!m) return fallback;\n              var h = m[1].length === 3 ? m[1].replace(/./g, \"$&$&\") : m[1];\n              return \"#\" + h.toLowerCase();\n            }\n            var tint = hex(vars.tint, \"#63e8ff\");\n            var glow = num(vars.glow, 1, 0, 3);\n            var ghost = num(vars.ghost, 1, 0, 3);\n            var flicker = num(vars.flicker, 1, 0, 3);\n            var intensity = num(vars.intensity, 1, 0, 1);\n            var resolution = num(vars.resolution, 0.75, 0.25, 1);\n            var title = str(vars.title, \"Deploys this week\");\n            var value = str(vars.value, \"2,481\");\n            var background = hex(vars.background, \"#0a0a0a\");\n            var accent = hex(vars.accent, \"#a1eebd\");\n            var tintRgb = [parseInt(tint.slice(1, 3), 16) / 255, parseInt(tint.slice(3, 5), 16) / 255, parseInt(tint.slice(5, 7), 16) / 255];\n\n            // ---- The scene: remocn's preview (CanvasSceneA, a stat and eight bars), laid out for 896 x 633 design pixels and scaled to the frame.\n            var W = Math.max(2, root.clientWidth);\n            var H = Math.max(2, root.clientHeight);\n            var cw = Math.max(2, Math.round(W * resolution));\n            var ch = Math.max(2, Math.round(H * resolution));\n            scene.width = cw;\n            scene.height = ch;\n            var SANS = \"Geist, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, sans-serif\";\n            var BARS = [0.32, 0.51, 0.43, 0.68, 0.57, 0.86, 0.64, 1];\n            function drawScene() {\n              var ctx = scene.getContext(\"2d\");\n              ctx.setTransform(cw / W, 0, 0, ch / H, 0, 0);\n              ctx.fillStyle = background;\n              ctx.fillRect(0, 0, W, H);\n              var s = Math.min(W / 896, H / 633);\n              var blockW = 8 * 74 * s + 7 * 16 * s;\n              var x0 = (W - blockW) / 2;\n              var titleH = 34 * 1.2 * s, valueH = 152 * s, barsH = 190 * s;\n              var total = titleH + 6 * s + valueH + 52 * s + barsH;\n              var y = (H - total) / 2;\n              ctx.textBaseline = \"alphabetic\";\n              ctx.textAlign = \"left\";\n              ctx.font = \"400 \" + 34 * s + \"px \" + SANS;\n              ctx.fillStyle = \"#8b8f9a\";\n              ctx.fillText(title, x0, y + titleH * 0.78);\n              y += titleH + 6 * s;\n              ctx.font = \"600 \" + 152 * s + \"px \" + SANS;\n              if (\"letterSpacing\" in ctx) ctx.letterSpacing = (-0.04 * 152 * s) + \"px\";\n              ctx.fillStyle = \"#f2f2f2\";\n              ctx.fillText(value, x0, y + valueH * 0.84);\n              if (\"letterSpacing\" in ctx) ctx.letterSpacing = \"0px\";\n              y += valueH + 52 * s;\n              BARS.forEach(function (b, i) {\n                var bx = x0 + i * (74 + 16) * s, bh = b * barsH;\n                ctx.fillStyle = i === BARS.length - 1 ? accent : \"#23262e\";\n                ctx.beginPath();\n                ctx.roundRect(bx, y + barsH - bh, 74 * s, bh, 10 * s);\n                ctx.fill();\n              });\n            }\n\n            // ---- remocn's shader (canvas-presentation vertex shader, hologram fragment shader).\n            var VERTEX = [\n              \"#version 300 es\",\n              \"in vec2 a_pos;\",\n              \"out vec2 v_uv;\",\n              \"void main() {\",\n              \"  v_uv = vec2(a_pos.x * 0.5 + 0.5, 0.5 - a_pos.y * 0.5);\",\n              \"  gl_Position = vec4(a_pos, 0.0, 1.0);\",\n              \"}\"\n            ].join(\"\\n\");\n            var FRAGMENT = [\n              \"#version 300 es\",\n              \"precision highp float;\",\n              \"\",\n              \"uniform sampler2D u_scene;\",\n              \"uniform float u_aspect;\",\n              \"uniform float u_frame;\",\n              \"uniform vec3 u_tint;\",\n              \"uniform float u_glow;\",\n              \"uniform float u_ghost;\",\n              \"uniform float u_flicker;\",\n              \"uniform float u_intensity;\",\n              \"\",\n              \"in vec2 v_uv;\",\n              \"out vec4 outColor;\",\n              \"\",\n              \"const float PI = 3.141592653589793;\",\n              \"const float TAU = 6.28318530718;\",\n              \"const float GOLDEN = 2.39996323;\",\n              \"const int HALO_TAPS = 8;\",\n              \"const vec3 LUMA = vec3(0.299, 0.587, 0.114);\",\n              \"\",\n              \"float hash(vec2 p) {\",\n              \"  return fract(sin(dot(p, vec2(12.9898, 78.233))) * 43758.5453123);\",\n              \"}\",\n              \"\",\n              \"float lumaAt(vec2 uv) {\",\n              \"  return dot(texture(u_scene, uv).rgb, LUMA);\",\n              \"}\",\n              \"\",\n              \"void main() {\",\n              \"  vec4 src = texture(u_scene, v_uv);\",\n              \"  float amount = clamp(u_intensity, 0.0, 1.0);\",\n              \"\",\n              \"  if (!(amount > 0.001)) {\",\n              \"    outColor = src;\",\n              \"    return;\",\n              \"  }\",\n              \"\",\n              \"  float row = floor(v_uv.y * 300.0);\",\n              \"  float clock = floor(u_frame);\",\n              \"  float slip =\",\n              \"    (hash(vec2(row, clock)) - 0.5) * u_ghost * 0.006 * step(0.55, hash(vec2(row, clock + 3.0)));\",\n              \"  vec2 base = vec2(v_uv.x + slip / u_aspect, v_uv.y);\",\n              \"\",\n              \"  vec4 held = texture(u_scene, base);\",\n              \"  float lit = dot(held.rgb, LUMA);\",\n              \"\",\n              \"  vec2 apart = vec2(u_ghost * 0.0045 / u_aspect, u_ghost * 0.0035);\",\n              \"  vec3 twin = texture(u_scene, base + apart).rgb;\",\n              \"\",\n              \"  float step2 = 0.0022;\",\n              \"  float gx =\",\n              \"    lumaAt(base + vec2(step2 / u_aspect, 0.0)) -\",\n              \"    lumaAt(base - vec2(step2 / u_aspect, 0.0));\",\n              \"  float gy = lumaAt(base + vec2(0.0, step2)) - lumaAt(base - vec2(0.0, step2));\",\n              \"  float rim = clamp(length(vec2(gx, gy)) * 7.0, 0.0, 1.0);\",\n              \"\",\n              \"  vec3 halo = vec3(0.0);\",\n              \"  for (int i = 0; i < HALO_TAPS; i++) {\",\n              \"    float angle = float(i) * GOLDEN;\",\n              \"    float reach = sqrt((float(i) + 0.5) / float(HALO_TAPS)) * u_glow * 0.022;\",\n              \"    vec2 at = base + vec2(cos(angle) * reach / u_aspect, sin(angle) * reach);\",\n              \"    halo += max(texture(u_scene, at).rgb - 0.34, vec3(0.0));\",\n              \"  }\",\n              \"  halo /= float(HALO_TAPS);\",\n              \"\",\n              \"  vec3 core = u_tint * (0.12 + lit * 1.55);\",\n              \"  core = mix(core, held.rgb * u_tint * 1.9, 0.12);\",\n              \"  core += u_tint * rim * 1.9 * u_glow;\",\n              \"  core += halo * u_tint * 2.4 * u_glow;\",\n              \"  core += twin * u_tint * 0.5 * u_ghost;\",\n              \"\",\n              \"  float interlace = mod(row, 2.0) < 1.0 ? 1.0 : 0.58;\",\n              \"  core *= interlace;\",\n              \"\",\n              \"  float blink =\",\n              \"    1.0 -\",\n              \"    u_flicker *\",\n              \"      (0.04 + 0.05 * hash(vec2(clock, 7.0))) *\",\n              \"      (0.5 + 0.5 * sin(u_frame * TAU / 15.0));\",\n              \"  core *= blink;\",\n              \"\",\n              \"  float presence = clamp(lit * 1.5 + rim * 0.8 + 0.03, 0.0, 1.0);\",\n              \"  vec3 painted = clamp(u_tint * 0.035 + core * presence, 0.0, 1.0);\",\n              \"\",\n              \"  outColor = vec4(mix(src.rgb, painted, amount), src.a);\",\n              \"}\"\n            ].join(\"\\n\");\n\n            canvas.width = cw;\n            canvas.height = ch;\n            var gl = canvas.getContext(\"webgl2\", { antialias: false, depth: false, stencil: false, preserveDrawingBuffer: true });\n            function compile(type, source) {\n              var shader = gl.createShader(type);\n              gl.shaderSource(shader, source);\n              gl.compileShader(shader);\n              if (!gl.getShaderParameter(shader, gl.COMPILE_STATUS)) throw new Error(gl.getShaderInfoLog(shader) || \"shader compile failed\");\n              return shader;\n            }\n            var paint = null;\n            var upload = function () {};\n            try {\n              if (!gl) throw new Error(\"WebGL2 is not available\");\n              var program = gl.createProgram();\n              gl.attachShader(program, compile(gl.VERTEX_SHADER, VERTEX));\n              gl.attachShader(program, compile(gl.FRAGMENT_SHADER, FRAGMENT));\n              gl.linkProgram(program);\n              if (!gl.getProgramParameter(program, gl.LINK_STATUS)) throw new Error(gl.getProgramInfoLog(program) || \"link failed\");\n              gl.useProgram(program);\n              var buffer = gl.createBuffer();\n              gl.bindBuffer(gl.ARRAY_BUFFER, buffer);\n              gl.bufferData(gl.ARRAY_BUFFER, new Float32Array([-1, -1, 1, -1, -1, 1, 1, 1]), gl.STATIC_DRAW);\n              var aPos = gl.getAttribLocation(program, \"a_pos\");\n              gl.enableVertexAttribArray(aPos);\n              gl.vertexAttribPointer(aPos, 2, gl.FLOAT, false, 0, 0);\n              var texture = gl.createTexture();\n              gl.activeTexture(gl.TEXTURE0);\n              gl.bindTexture(gl.TEXTURE_2D, texture);\n              gl.texParameteri(gl.TEXTURE_2D, gl.TEXTURE_WRAP_S, gl.CLAMP_TO_EDGE);\n              gl.texParameteri(gl.TEXTURE_2D, gl.TEXTURE_WRAP_T, gl.CLAMP_TO_EDGE);\n              gl.texParameteri(gl.TEXTURE_2D, gl.TEXTURE_MIN_FILTER, gl.LINEAR);\n              gl.texParameteri(gl.TEXTURE_2D, gl.TEXTURE_MAG_FILTER, gl.LINEAR);\n              gl.viewport(0, 0, cw, ch);\n              function u(name) { return gl.getUniformLocation(program, name); }\n              gl.uniform1i(u(\"u_scene\"), 0);\n              gl.uniform1f(u(\"u_aspect\"), cw / ch);\n              gl.uniform3fv(u(\"u_tint\"), tintRgb);\n              gl.uniform1f(u(\"u_glow\"), glow);\n              gl.uniform1f(u(\"u_ghost\"), ghost);\n              gl.uniform1f(u(\"u_flicker\"), flicker);\n              gl.uniform1f(u(\"u_intensity\"), intensity);\n              var frameLoc = u(\"u_frame\");\n              upload = function () {\n                gl.texImage2D(gl.TEXTURE_2D, 0, gl.RGBA, gl.RGBA, gl.UNSIGNED_BYTE, scene);\n              };\n              paint = function (frame) {\n                gl.uniform1f(frameLoc, frame);\n                gl.clearColor(0, 0, 0, 0);\n                gl.clear(gl.COLOR_BUFFER_BIT);\n                gl.drawArrays(gl.TRIANGLE_STRIP, 0, 4);\n              };\n            } catch (err) {\n              stage.classList.add(\"hol-off\");\n              if (window.console) console.warn(NAME + \":\", err.message);\n            }\n\n            // The scene is redrawn whenever a web font finishes loading, so no frame keeps a fallback face.\n            var fontEpoch = 0;\n            var sceneEpoch = -1;\n            var lastFrame = 0;\n            function render(frame) {\n              lastFrame = frame;\n              if (sceneEpoch !== fontEpoch) {\n                sceneEpoch = fontEpoch;\n                drawScene();\n                upload();\n              }\n              if (paint) paint(frame);\n            }\n            if (document.fonts && document.fonts.load) {\n              [\"400 34px Geist\", \"600 152px Geist\"].forEach(function (face) {\n                document.fonts.load(face).then(function () { fontEpoch++; render(lastFrame); }, function () {});\n              });\n            }\n            var tl = gsap.timeline({ paused: true });\n            var totalFrames = Math.round(total * 30);\n            var clock = { frame: 0 };\n            tl.to(clock, { frame: totalFrames, duration: total, ease: \"none\", onUpdate: function () { render(Math.round(clock.frame)); } }, 0);\n            render(0);\n            if (tl.duration() < total) tl.to({}, { duration: total - tl.duration() });\n            tl.seek(0);\n            window.__timelines = window.__timelines || {};\n            window.__timelines[\"hologram\"] = tl;\n          })();\n        </script>\n      </div>\n    </template>\n  </body>\n</html>\n"
  }
 ],
 "sha256": "33ad65c46ddedc4a108ae8effa649ef5f11cb79bddcb62f7ce6ea801368f4713",
